c-article-history-item__doi" data-test="revision-doi">
                            DOI:
                            <span>https://doi.org/10.12942/lrr-2014-4</span></p><div class="c-article-history-item__changelog"><aside>
              
                <h3 class="c-article__sub-heading">Change summary</h3>
                <p>Major revision, updated and expanded.</p>
              
              
                <h3 class="c-article__sub-heading">Change details</h3>
                <p>Added new Section <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec2.3.3">2.3.3</a> on the Pioneer anomaly; split former Section <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec3">3</a> into new <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec3">3</a> and <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec4">4</a>, and extended Section <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec3.3">3.3</a> on competing theories of gravity; added new Sections <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec5.3">5.3</a> and <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec5.4">5.4</a> on compact binary systems; added a new Section <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="section anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Sec8">8</a> on astrophysical and cosmological tests.</p>
                <p>The number of references increased from 299 to 454. Added two figures (<a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig8">8</a>, <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig9">9</a>) and updated Figures <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig1">1</a>, <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig3">3</a>, <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig5">5</a>, and <a data-track="click" data-track-label="link" data-track-action="figure anchor" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2014-4#Fig7">7</a>.</p>
              
            </aside></div></li><li class="c-article-history-item"><a class="c-article-history-item__title" data-test="title" href="/article/10.12942/lrr-2006-3"><span>The Confrontation between General Relativity and Experiment</span></a><ul class="c-article-history-item__authors"><li data-test="author-name">Clifford M. Will</li></ul><dl class="c-article-history-item__dates"><dt>Published:</dt><dd data-test="published-date">27 March 2006</dd><dt>Accepted:</dt><dd data-test="accepted-date">27 February 2006</dd></dl><p class="c-article-history-item__doi" data-test="revision-doi">
